<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'FAQ' }) %>

<div class="row justify-content-center">
  <div class="col-lg-9">
    <h1 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-patch-question text-primary"></i> Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mb-4">
      Quick answers about accounts, connections, jobs and privacy.
      Still stuck? <a href="/contact">Send us a message</a> — we usually
      reply within 2 working days.
    </p>

    <div class="accordion shadow-sm" id="faqAccordion">

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq1">
            How do I create an account?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Click <strong>Register</strong>, fill in your name, email and a
            password, and choose your role — <strong>Student</strong>,
            <strong>Alumni</strong> or <strong>Faculty</strong>. Then log in
            with the same email and password. After your first login, open
            <strong>Edit Profile</strong> and complete your details (course
            or company, skills, bio, photo) so other members can find and
            recognise you.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq2">
            Who can join Alumni Hub?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Current <strong>students</strong>, passed-out
            <strong>alumni</strong> and <strong>faculty</strong> members of
            the institute. An <strong>admin</strong> from the Alumni Cell
            manages the platform and can block or remove accounts that
            misuse it.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq3">
            How do I connect with someone?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Open the <strong>Members</strong> directory, find the person
            (you can type in the search box or filter by role) and click
            <strong>Connect</strong>. They get a notification and can accept
            or reject your request from their
            <strong>Connections</strong> page. Once you are connected, you
            can also message each other from the <strong>Chat</strong> page.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq4">
            What are the "Suggested for You" recommendations on my dashboard?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Alumni Hub compares your profile with every other member —
            course/domain, skills, interests, batch and city — and suggests
            the people most similar to you, with a match percentage and the
            reasons (for example, "3 common skills"). Students also see job
            suggestions matched to their skills. The more complete your
            profile is, the better the suggestions become.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq5">
            Who can post jobs, and how do I apply for one?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <strong>Alumni</strong> post jobs and internships from the
            <strong>Jobs</strong> page. <strong>Students</strong> open a job,
            click <strong>Apply</strong> and can add a short cover note.
            The alumnus reviews applicants and updates each application to
            <strong>Shortlisted</strong> or <strong>Rejected</strong>;
            students follow the status live under
            <strong>My Applications</strong> and get a notification on
            every change.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq6">
            How do announcements work?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <strong>Faculty</strong> members publish announcements — alumni
            meets, events, deadlines and notices — from the
            <strong>Announcements</strong> page. Every logged-in member can
            read them, and the dashboard shows how many announcements have
            been posted.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq7">
            How do I update my profile or change my password?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Click your name in the top-right corner and choose
            <strong>Edit Profile</strong> to update your phone, photo,
            skills, bio and role details. In the same menu,
            <strong>Change Password</strong> lets you set a new password —
            you will be asked for the current one first.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#faq8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq8">
            Is my information private?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="faq8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Profiles are visible only to <strong>logged-in members</strong>
            of the institute — guests see only the public pages. Passwords
            are never stored in plain text; they are saved as secure
            one-way hashes. Your email address is shown to fellow members
            so they can reach you; do not share your password with anyone,
            including anyone claiming to be the admin.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm mt-4">
      <div class="card-body d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-3">
        <i class="bi bi-envelope-paper fs-2 text-primary"></i>
        <div class="flex-grow-1">
          <strong>Didn't find your answer?</strong><br>
          <span class="text-muted">The Alumni Cell team reads every message sent from the Contact page.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">
          <i class="bi bi-send"></i> Contact Us
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
